		<defName>Anneli_Faction_Ahmislan</defName>
		<label>Anneli Faction Ahmislan Kingdom</label>
		<description>Once a famous interplanetary medieval theme park, the Ahmislan Kingdom eventually went bankrupt. The tourists left, but the employees remained. Armed with survival training, replica tools, and a manual titled "Living in a Medieval Society", they somehow kept the kingdom running for real.\n\nThe park soon attracted a new population: vagrants, doomsday cultists, isekai travelers, and armored-combat enthusiasts—anyone who found modern civilization terribly boring. Shantytowns spilled past the gift shops, foam castles were reinforced into real fortresses, and seasonal performers gradually became hereditary high nobility.\n\nUnfortunately, Ahmislan remained far better at being medieval than being functional. Modern technology was banned for breaking immersion and economic reform was endlessly postponed because most of the kingdom’s revenue had already been spent on far more interesting things like grand tournaments, crusades, and sacred quests for the Holy Grail.\n\nThe kingdom is on the verge of collapse, filled with bankrupt farmers, insufferable mercenaries, and idling knights preparing to draw steel over the slightest offense. The rulers are not particularly concerned, seeing both prosperity and doom as part of their story.</description>
